<title>BELGIUM: Spadel says Portuguese bottler restarts.</title>
<headline>Spadel says Portuguese bottler restarts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian beverage firm Spadel said on Thursday its Portuguese mineral water bottling unit Empresa das Aguas do Alardo would resume sales of its Alardo brand after clearance by health laboratories.</p>
<p>Bottles of Alardo were withdrawn from the shelves in Portugal on March 10 after traces of algae were found in some of them.</p>
<p>Spadel said in a statement that tests in laboratories in Portugal, France and Belgium had found the water to be clear for consumption. Bottling had therefore restarted on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
